A||||1||NEFA||Lebanon, NH show this weekend||||1||
Z||000000||NEFA||08-14-2001||11:01 AM||||NEFA will have it's own Fiero class again this year. The show date is August 18th at Colburn Park in Lebanon, NH (same place as last years) and runs from 9am to 3pm, though people can start showing up even earlier than 9am if they like.<P>Bob Parker of Kick Hill Farms is the sponsor for the Fiero class again this year. We are going to hopefully have a cool Ratty Fiero trophy class at the show also, sponsored by a local auto place.<P>Steve Kelley and family will also have their now annual Fiero cookout at their place in Plainfield, NH after the show.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fieropride.com/logos/NEFA_Logo12_small.gif">   <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieropride.com/calendar.htm" TARGET=_blank>Upcoming Club Events</A> <P><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/jaygee79/tshirt.html" TARGET=_blank>Get your Club T-shirt</A>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Fiero5||08-14-2001||11:37 PM||||There is also the Fiero Dutch Classic II in PA, so either way we have Fiero lovers covered for shows this weekend in the North East area of the country.<BR>You can check the calendar of events on the wwwfieropride.com web site - or-<BR>For more info on the Lebanon NH show, just e-mail me at:<BR>stevekelley@nhvt.net<BR>For more info on the Fiero Dutch Classic II, e-mail the MAFOA president Bob Schlag at:<BR>bobschlag@fieropride.com<P>The Lebanon NH show is a big car show with a Fiero class. The Fiero Dutch classic is just Fieros.<P>If you can't make the PA show, we look forward to hopefully seeing you at the Lebanon NH show and then the 7 mile drive to our place after for the now famouse Kelley Fiero cookout at 4pm.<BR>We are also just a few miles from the longest covered bridge in the US that crosses from Cornish NH to Windsor VT. A great Photo oportunity to have a pic of your beautiful Fiero next to this old historic two span long covered bridge!<P>See ya there!<P>Steve||||reg||10
